; fas9_contexts.scr - facit of step 9.17 (F9.19: the annotation contexts, ObjectContext/AnnotScale bases; F9.8's DIMASSOC part is in
; fas9_special_dimensions.scr).
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_contexts.scr
; starts AutoCAD 2025's core on acad.dwt (a new empty drawing). Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (see fas9_example.scr).
;
; What is made: an ANNOTATIVE text style (-STYLE _Annotative) and an ANNOTATIVE dimension style (-DIMSTYLE _Annotative), two extra
; scales (-SCALELISTEDIT: HDXF_1_2 and HDXF_1_5), CANNOSCALE 1:1, and annotative TEXT (one rotated), MTEXT, linear, aligned, angular,
; radius, diameter and ordinate dimensions, DIMJOGGED, DIMARC, LEADER, MLEADER, a hatch (HPANNOTATIVE 1: HATCHSCALE and HATCHVIEW
; contexts; one with a dashed pattern), and an annotative block with its INSERT (BLKREF). -OBJECTSCALE adds the two scales to every
; annotative object: each has three contexts (1:1 the default, 1:2, 1:5).
;   contexts                      the drawing so
;   contexts rotated              the second TEXT rotated 30 degrees (the contexts of the other scales)
;   contexts leader_stretched     a vertex of the LEADER moved (its contexts' point lists)
;   contexts autoscale            ANNOAUTOSCALE 1 and CANNOSCALE HDXF_1_5 after a scale 1:10 was added to the list: what AutoCAD adds
;   contexts scale_removed        -OBJECTSCALE _Delete HDXF_1_5 from every object (the 1:5 contexts and their dictionary entries go)
;   contexts scale_list_deleted   -SCALELISTEDIT _Delete HDXF_1_2 (a scale the objects still use) and _Delete of the unused one
; MLEADER is made with the command (text on the command line); its style Standard is not annotative and the core has no MLEADERSTYLE command
; (-MLEADERSTYLE is unknown to it), so its contexts are only in Erik's acad_<version>_dxf_annotative*.dxf (setpropertyvalue Annotative).
; Not made here (plan 9.17, "Ej testat", F9.19): ACDB_ANNOTSCALEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA_CLASS as a record of its own (AutoCAD writes the
; base only inside the concrete classes: it has no 0 record in any file), the MTEXTATTRIBUTE and FCF contexts are in Erik's
; acad_<version>_dxf_annotative*.dxf (14_annotative.scr: the core's ATTDEF has no multiple-line attribute and its TOLERANCE is a dialog),
; an annotative object in paper space and in a block (BLKREF inside a block), grips for a context's own point.
